From b5ce41083f03123af65caab2cceef07a41bd16c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "iLinux local research (AI-generated draft)" <local@invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:06:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] arm64: dts: apple: Add draft t6050 (M5 Max) J716c device
 tree

Draft device tree for the MacBook Pro 16-inch M5 Max (Mac17,6, J716c),
generated by kernel/experiments/t6050-dt/gen_t6050_dt.py from a
sanitized macOS ADT capture of that machine:

  - 18 CPUs (2 x 6 M cores, 1 x 6 P cores) with MPIDR-based reg values
    (M: 0x40000|cluster<<8|core, P: 0x10000|cluster<<8|core, from m1n1
    commit 5d84c4c34d3f), L2 caches, cpu-map
  - per-cluster OPP tables from the PMGR voltage-states tables selected by
    acc-clusters (M: 15 states 1.344-4.380 GHz, P: 20 states
    1.308-4.608 GHz) and cluster cpufreq controllers; opp-microvolt and
    dynamic-power-coefficient / capacity-dmips-mhz for an energy model
    (the latter two are hypotheses derived from macOS IOReport energy
    measurements and must be re-measured natively)
  - AIC3, arch timer, watchdog, 3 pinctrl blocks, 9 I2C, UART0
  - 188 PMGR power domains in 6 PMGR blocks (t6050-pmgr.dtsi), decoded
    from the ADT devices/ps-groups tables with the record layout
    documented in m1n1 proxyclient/m1n1/adt.py
  - disabled draft nodes for the t8110 DARTs, the SARTv4, the ANS
    mailbox and NVMe (M4+ register split)

Never booted.  Needs m1n1 with t6050 support; SMP is not functional in
m1n1 on t6050 yet, so m1n1 will prune all secondary CPU nodes.
Recommended extra kernel arguments for a first boot:
pd_ignore_unused clk_ignore_unused (m1n1 adds idle=nop arm64.nowfxt).

Status: compile-tested with dtc 1.8.1 (0 warnings) outside the kernel
tree only; dtbs_check pending.

2026-10-16 update: add the SMC and its mailbox.  smc@28c600000
(apple,t6050-smc, apple,t8103-smc; "smc" = the ASC block, "sram" = ASC +
0x1a00000 with 1 MiB as on t8103/t8122/t6031) and mbox@28c608000
(apple,t6050-asc-mailbox, interrupts 899-902 sorted from the ADT), with
gpio and hwmon subnodes.  The smc node stays status = "disabled" until a
native session verifies the transport; the reboot and rtc subnodes wait
for the SPMI PMU node that provides their nvmem cells.  Evidence: ADT
/arm-io/smc (iop,ascwrap-v6, role SMC, four mailbox interrupts, no power
gates) and offline analysis of this Mac's AppleSMC kext, which shows the
RTKit endpoint (0x20) and message layout the Linux macsmc driver
implements (iLinux kernel/experiments/smc/README.md).  apple,t6050-smc
is not yet documented in bindings/mfd/apple,smc.yaml (file outside the
sparse checkout), so dtbs_check will flag the first compatible.

NOT FOR UPSTREAM SUBMISSION: AI-generated local research draft (Asahi
Linux generative-AI policy).  No Signed-off-by on purpose.

